I could not reproduce the reported outage. Inter-campus reachability from multiple Campus 1 VLANs (172.16.10.x, 172.16.20.x, 172.16.30.x) to Campus 2 subnets (10.5.0.x and 10.6.0.x) is currently healthy. Evidence: from pc5 (172.16.10.5) pings to 10.5.0.1/10.5.0.2 and 10.6.0.3/10.6.0.4 all returned 0% loss with ~1.7–2.5 ms RTT. From pc12 (172.16.30.12) to 10.5.0.1/10.5.0.2 and 10.6.0.3/10.6.0.4 also 0% loss with ~1.5–2.8 ms RTT. From pc9 (172.16.20.9) to 10.5.0.2 and 10.6.0.3 likewise 0% loss, sub-3 ms RTT. The topology-wide reachability matrix also shows consistent bi-directional connectivity between these networks.

Affected component: none; no subsystem/daemon/interface/policy is currently misconfigured or failing. Mechanism: because routing and L2/L3 forwarding across the inter-campus path are functioning, traffic reaches Campus 2 normally with low latency and no loss. Localization: tests cover hosts across all three Campus 1 VLANs to multiple hosts in both Campus 2 subnets, indicating no localized or path-specific failure. Root cause: not reproducible at this time; if there was an earlier issue, it was transient and has self-cleared.

Corrective fix: no changes required. Recommend monitoring for recurrence (collect interface errors and routing logs on the inter-campus routers/switch uplinks). If it recurs, capture ping/traceroute and timestamps to correlate with device logs for precise root-cause isolation.
